@startuml state-lifecycle
!include _style.iuml
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
  FontSize 12
}
title Incident lifecycle (as implemented in IncidentStates)

[*] --> NEW : report()\nIncidentFactory.create
NEW --> CLASSIFIED : classify()\n[category != null]
NEW --> CANCELLED : cancel()\nreporter / admin
CLASSIFIED --> ASSIGNED : assignTo()\nauto strategy, manual, take\n[assignee != null]
CLASSIFIED --> CANCELLED : cancel()
ASSIGNED --> ACKNOWLEDGED : acknowledge()\n/ sla.markResponded
ACKNOWLEDGED --> IN_PROGRESS : start()
IN_PROGRESS --> AWAITING_INFO : requestInfo()
AWAITING_INFO --> IN_PROGRESS : provideInfo() / start()
IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED : resolve()\n[resolution present]\n/ sla.markResolved
AWAITING_INFO --> RESOLVED : resolve()
RESOLVED --> VERIFIED : verify(rating 1-5)\nreporter / admin
RESOLVED --> REOPENED : reopen(reason)\n/ sla.reopen
REOPENED --> ASSIGNED : back to same technician\nor auto-assign
VERIFIED --> CLOSED : close()\n/ closedAt set
CLOSED --> [*]
CANCELLED --> [*]

note right of CLASSIFIED
  Priority + SLA clock are set here
  (applyPriority). Reassignment is allowed in
  CLASSIFIED, ASSIGNED, ACKNOWLEDGED,
  IN_PROGRESS, AWAITING_INFO, REOPENED.
end note
note left of NEW
  Any other move, e.g. NEW -> CLOSED,
  throws InvalidStateTransitionException
  (HTTP 409 INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION).
end note
@enduml
